NativeSupporterVault::deposit (shared by RethSupporterVault and YsyBoldSupporterVault)
├── Given recovery has begun
│   └── It reverts without accepting custody or reopening the terminal vault
├── Given deadline expired, entries disabled, or report invalid/stale
│   └── It reverts before recording a position
├── Given either bucket has an economic deficit or physical custody is short
│   └── It blocks the whole affected leg but not the sibling token vault
├── Given transfer has a fee, fails, or reenters
│   └── It rolls back balances, IDs and basis
├── Given zero quantity/value, insufficient minimum, or zero immediate inverse payout
│   └── It rejects the dust trap without consuming funds
└── Given exact native tokens and valid accounting
    ├── When canonical supply is zero
    │   └── It follows the external protocol's one-to-one convention
    ├── When there is existing carry or unsolicited surplus
    │   └── It credits only this entry's floor-rounded recognized basis
    └── It creates a new caller-owned, nontransferable ID with a 30-day lock
